     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-09-24 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Breaking Barriers: Two Women Cycle Through Age Stereotypes</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cycling</span> <span>#Women</span> <span>#Inspiration</span> <span>#Empowerment</span></div>
       <p>Renu Singhi, 58, from Jaipur, and Gareema Shankar, 44, from Delhi, are challenging societal norms through their passion for cycling. Renu begins her day with a 70 km ride, a routine she embraced after buying her first cycle at 52. Her motivation is simple: &quot;For once, I am doing something for myself and not for anyone else.&quot; She inspired Gareema, who initially cycled in secret, wary of others' opinions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/breaking-barriers-two-women-cycle-through-age-stereotypes.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Gareema’s perspective shifted after learning about Renu's journey on a Zoom call in 2021, prompting her to ask, &quot;What's stopping you?&quot; The duo's unique friendship blossomed when they met at the London-Edinburgh-London (LEL) challenge in 2022. Renu, a star at the event, had previously completed the 1,200 km Paris-Brest-Paris (PBP) in a remarkable 92 hours.</p><p>Gareema, despite a setback at LEL, trained rigorously and completed the PBP challenge in 98 hours in August 2023, crediting failure as her biggest teacher. These women exemplify how dedication and self-belief can overcome perceived limitations, proving that age is truly just a number when pursuing personal passions.</p><p>Why it matters: Their stories inspire countless others to pursue their passions regardless of age or societal expectations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Faithful to source; no invented information.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/329462/gareema-shankar-and-renu-singhi-cycling-journey-paris-brest-paris-women-friendship/" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
