     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-09-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Everything new coming to Meta&amp;#8217;s AI agent Muse</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Meta</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#Muse</span> <span>#Mark Zuckerberg</span></div>
       <p>Meta is making a significant push into artificial intelligence, with CEO Mark Zuckerberg highlighting the company's &quot;all-in&quot; strategy on its AI agent, Muse. The announcement came during Meta's annual Connect event, held on Wednesday in Menlo Park, where Zuckerberg delivered a keynote address outlining the company's future direction in AI.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/everything-new-coming-to-meta8217s-ai-agent-muse.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>A key revelation from the event is the expansion of Muse's integration across Meta's product ecosystem. Notably, the AI agent is slated to arrive on Meta's AI glasses, signaling a move towards embedding advanced AI capabilities directly into wearable technology. This integration suggests a vision where AI becomes a more seamless and interactive part of users' daily lives, extending beyond traditional screens.</p><p>The focus on Muse at the Connect event underscores Meta's commitment to developing and deploying sophisticated AI tools. By integrating Muse into its AI glasses, Meta is positioning itself to explore new frontiers in augmented reality and personalized AI assistance. This strategic direction indicates a future where AI agents like Muse will play an increasingly central role in how users interact with Meta's platforms and devices.</p><p>What to watch: The practical applications and user experience of Muse on Meta's AI glasses.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article conveys the key points of the source summary accurately and professionally.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/23/everything-new-coming-to-metas-ai-agent-muse/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
