       <h1>Flying Wedge Defence &amp; Aerospace completes 100 flight-test - Bisinfotech</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Aerospace</span> <span>#Flight Test</span> <span>#Flying Wedge Defence &amp; Aerospace</span></div>
       <p>Flying Wedge Defence &amp; Aerospace has achieved a notable milestone, successfully completing its 100th flight test. This accomplishment was reported by Bisinfotech, highlighting a significant benchmark for the aerospace and defence entity.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/flying-wedge-defence-aerospace-completes-100-flight-test-bis.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The completion of 100 flight tests indicates a sustained period of development, evaluation, and operational trials for Flying Wedge Defence &amp; Aerospace. Such rigorous testing is a critical phase in the development cycle of any aerospace platform or system, ensuring performance, reliability, and safety standards are met.</p><p>While specific details regarding the nature of the aircraft or systems undergoing these tests were not elaborated in the report, the sheer volume of flight tests suggests a robust and active research and development program. Reaching a triple-digit flight test count is often seen as an indicator of progress in validating designs, technologies, and operational capabilities within the defence and aerospace sectors.</p><p>This milestone contributes to the company's profile within the defence aggregate, underscoring its commitment to advancing its aerospace capabilities through methodical testing. The achievement, as reported, marks a significant operational benchmark for Flying Wedge Defence &amp; Aerospace in its ongoing efforts.</p><p>What to watch: Any future announcements detailing the specific projects or outcomes of these flight tests.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reports on the milestone achieved by Flying Wedge Defence &amp; Aerospace as noted in the source.</p>
