     <article class="story single" data-beat="environment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Guardian Environment · 2026-09-24 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Fossil Fuel Industry Secured $190 Billion in Benefits After Trump's Donation Call, Report Alleges</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#fossil fuels</span> <span>#tax breaks</span> <span>#subsidies</span> <span>#Donald Trump</span></div>
       <p>A new report by Senator Sheldon Whitehouse and Senate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer alleges that the fossil fuel industry secured an estimated $190 billion in tax breaks and subsidies over the next decade. This substantial financial benefit reportedly followed the industry's response to Donald Trump's pre-election call for major campaign donations.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/fossil-fuel-industry-secured-190-billion-in-benefits-after-t.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Released on Thursday, the report asserts that American taxpayers are now facing higher bills and increased public health costs directly associated with pollution. The senators describe this outcome as a 'bargain' struck between the former president and major polluters, highlighting what they term the fossil fuel industry’s expansive influence over the Trump administration.</p><p>The $190 billion figure represents projected benefits spanning a ten-year period, according to the findings presented by Senator Whitehouse, who is the ranking member of the Senate environment and public works committee, and Senator Schumer. Their report underscores concerns about the financial implications for the public and the environmental impact attributed to these arrangements. The document details the alleged extent of the industry's sway within the previous administration.</p><p>What to watch: Congressional and public responses to the report's findings and future policy debates.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Faithful to source; no invented information.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/24/fossil-fuels-trump-donations" rel="noopener">Guardian Environment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
