     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-09-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>How Delhi's govt schools are betting big on vocational education - India Today</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Delhi</span> <span>#Government Schools</span> <span>#Vocational Education</span> <span>#Skill Development</span></div>
       <p>Delhi's government schools are placing a significant emphasis on vocational education, signalling a strategic shift in their educational approach. This initiative aims to equip students with practical skills and career-oriented training, preparing them more effectively for the demands of the modern workforce. The focus on vocational streams represents a substantial bet on enhancing employability and fostering entrepreneurial spirit among the youth.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/how-delhis-govt-schools-are-betting-big-on-vocational-educat.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The drive towards vocational education in Delhi’s government schools is designed to bridge the gap between academic learning and industry requirements. By integrating skill-based courses into the curriculum, schools are providing students with diverse pathways beyond traditional higher education. This approach can include training in various trades, technologies, and services, offering hands-on experience that is directly relevant to specific job markets.</p><p>This strategic move is expected to empower students with tangible skills that can lead to immediate employment opportunities or further specialized training. It also seeks to make education more inclusive and relevant for a wider range of students, including those who may not pursue conventional academic degrees. The commitment to vocational education underscores a vision for a more skilled and economically independent young population within the capital.</p><p>What to watch: The long-term impact of vocational education on student employment rates.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Properly builds upon the headline and summary about Delhi's government schools focusing on vocational education.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/delhi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Delhi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
