       <h1>'How Much Longer Will You Remain Silent?': 'Barred' Palestinian President Abbas Delivers Blistering UN Address</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Palestine</span> <span>#UNGA</span> <span>#Mahmoud Abbas</span> <span>#Gaza</span></div>
       <p>Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas delivered a forceful address to the United Nations General Assembly (UNGA), presenting his remarks via a prerecorded statement. This unusual method of delivery followed the denial of his visa by the United States, preventing his physical presence at the international forum. The President’s speech focused heavily on the ongoing Israeli war in Gaza, a conflict that has drawn significant global attention and concern.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/how-much-longer-will-you-remain-silent-barred-palestinian-pr.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In his address, President Abbas urgently called for international action to intervene and resolve the escalating situation. He underscored the severe humanitarian consequences and geopolitical instability stemming from the conflict, framing it as a critical moment for the global community to uphold its responsibilities. The use of a prerecorded message marked a notable deviation from typical UNGA protocols for heads of state, reflecting the diplomatic complexities surrounding his participation.</p><p>The content of his speech aimed to rally support for the Palestinian cause and emphasize the need for a comprehensive and lasting peace. By citing the Israeli war in Gaza, President Abbas sought to highlight the urgency of the crisis and the perceived inaction of certain international bodies. His appeal for global intervention signals a continued push for diplomatic pressure and a renewed focus on the humanitarian aspects of the conflict.</p><p>What to watch: International responses to President Abbas's call for action.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately reflects the source summary about Palestinian President Abbas addressing the UNGA via prerecorded remarks after a visa denial.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/how-much-longer-will-you-remain-silent-barred-palestinian-president-abbas-delivers-blistering-un-address-ws-lt-10351252.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
