       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-09-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India Must Build Critical Defence Systems At Home: CDS N.S. Raja Subramani</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Indigenous Production</span> <span>#National Security</span></div>
       <p>India's Chief of Defence Staff (CDS), N.S. Raja Subramani, has issued a clear directive advocating for the domestic development of critical defence systems. The CDS underscored the imperative for India to build these essential capabilities within its borders, a move that signals a reinforced commitment to self-reliance in national security matters. This strategic emphasis aims to ensure the nation's defence preparedness and technological sovereignty.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/india-must-build-critical-defence-systems-at-home-cds-ns-raj.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The statement, as reported by News18, highlights a pivotal shift towards indigenous production across the defence spectrum. By focusing on creating critical hardware and software systems at home, India intends to reduce its reliance on external sources, thereby strengthening its strategic autonomy. This approach is deemed crucial for safeguarding national interests and for responding effectively to evolving security challenges.</p><p>Developing these systems domestically offers several advantages, including tailored solutions, secure supply chains, and the fostering of a robust defence industrial ecosystem. The call from CDS N.S. Raja Subramani reinforces ongoing efforts to empower Indian industry and research institutions to contribute significantly to the nation's defence infrastructure. This direction is expected to guide future procurement policies and technological investments.</p><p>What to watch: Future policy announcements and initiatives bolstering domestic defence manufacturing.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source's primary message regarding the need for domestic defense development.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
