       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · BBC Health · 2026-09-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Linc Provides Free Counselling for Blood Cancer Patients in Gloucester</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#health</span> <span>#cancer</span> <span>#support</span></div>
       <p>Linc is offering free counselling sessions to individuals diagnosed with blood cancer, as well as their loved ones. The service is available to patients at any stage of their diagnosis, ensuring support is accessible whether someone is newly diagnosed, undergoing treatment, or navigating long-term care. Sessions can be conducted either online or in-person at The Forum in Gloucester, providing flexibility for those who may have mobility issues or prefer the comfort of home. This initiative aims to address the psychological and emotional challenges often accompanying a serious diagnosis, recognizing that mental health support is a critical component of overall patient care. By including loved ones in the scope of the service, Linc acknowledges the broader impact of blood cancer on families and support networks. The availability of these sessions at no cost removes financial barriers that might otherwise prevent individuals from seeking necessary help. This approach underscores the importance of holistic care in managing chronic and serious illnesses. Patients and their families are encouraged to reach out to access these resources, which are designed to provide a safe space for processing emotions and developing coping strategies. The service is currently active and open to those affected by blood cancer in the region, with no prerequisites other than the diagnosis itself. This effort highlights the growing recognition of the intersection between physical treatment and mental well-being in oncology care.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/linc-provides-free-counselling-for-blood-cancer-patients-in-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>What to watch: The uptake of online versus in-person sessions to gauge patient preference and accessibility.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate and well-written expansion of the provided BBC Health summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
