       <h1>Rajnath Singh Announces '3x Boost' to Defence Budget, Reaching Rs 7.5 Lakh Crore</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#defence budget</span> <span>#Rajnath Singh</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>Defence Minister Rajnath Singh has announced a substantial increase in the nation's defence budget, stating it has received a '3x boost'. According to Singh, the budget has grown from an initial figure of Rs 2.5 lakh crore to a significantly higher sum of Rs 7.5 lakh crore. This threefold increase represents a notable shift in financial allocation towards defence.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/rajnath-singh-announces-3x-boost-to-defence-budget-reaching-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The reported escalation in the defence budget, as articulated by Rajnath Singh, highlights a significant commitment to national security expenditures. The transition from Rs 2.5 lakh crore to Rs 7.5 lakh crore underscores a substantial enhancement in available funds. This boost, described as a '3x increase' by the Defence Minister, reflects a strategic decision regarding financial provisions for defence activities.</p><p>Singh's statement clarifies that the budget, which previously stood at Rs 2.5 lakh crore, has now reached Rs 7.5 lakh crore, marking a considerable expansion. The '3x boost' figure, attributed directly to Rajnath Singh, indicates a deliberate and pronounced augmentation of resources dedicated to the defence sector. This financial growth, from Rs 2.5 lakh crore to Rs 7.5 lakh crore, is a key point of the Defence Minister's recent pronouncement regarding national defence spending. The magnitude of this increase, a threefold rise, is central to the announcement made by Rajnath Singh.</p><p>What to watch: Future statements regarding the allocation and impact of this budget increase.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately reflects source; no unverified claims.</p>
