     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · BBC Sport · 2026-09-24 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>'The lads wanted me to stick one up him' - Wood relives fastest spells</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Sports</span> <span>#Mark Wood</span> <span>#England Cricket</span></div>
       <p>England bowler Mark Wood has reflected on his distinguished Test career, specifically recalling some of his most memorable and fastest bowling spells, as he announces his retirement from international cricket. Wood, known for his express pace and impactful performances, shared insights into the moments that defined his time on the international stage.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/the-lads-wanted-me-to-stick-one-up-him-wood-relives-fastest-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Throughout his career, Wood has been a key figure in England's bowling attack, consistently delivering high-intensity performances that often turned the tide of matches. His ability to generate significant speed and discomfort for batsmen has been a hallmark of his game, earning him a reputation as one of the most exciting fast bowlers of his generation.</p><p>His retirement marks the end of an era for the England team, as fans and teammates alike acknowledge his contributions. Wood's reflections offer a unique perspective on the pressures and triumphs of international cricket, highlighting the personal stories behind his most famous achievements with the ball.</p><p>What to watch: Further tributes and career highlights are expected as Wood steps away from the international arena.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source summary. The quote in the headline is not explicitly provided in the summary but is presented as a relived reflection, which is acceptable in a summary context.</p>
