     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-09-24 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>U.S., China Share 'Historic Responsibility' for Human Development, Says Xi Amid White House Welcome</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#US-China Relations</span> <span>#Diplomacy</span> <span>#International Relations</span> <span>#President Trump</span></div>
       <p>President Trump extended a formal welcome to President Xi at the White House, an event that saw both leaders engage in high-level discussions. During the welcome, President Trump spoke of a significant personal bond, stating that he and President Xi had &quot;forged a friendship, a truly great friendship, actually,&quot; since his first election in 2016. He further characterized this relationship as being &quot;built on mutual respect and the vital interests of our people,&quot; underscoring the foundation of their ongoing dialogue.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/us-china-share-historic-responsibility-for-human-development.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This high-profile interaction comes as President Xi articulated a view on the broader roles of their respective nations. According to reports, President Xi affirmed that the United States and China bear a &quot;historic responsibility&quot; to further human development. This statement sets a tone for cooperative potential, even amidst complex geopolitical dynamics. The exchange at the White House highlights the continued importance of direct engagement between the leaders of the world's two largest economies. The formal reception underscores the diplomatic efforts to manage relations and address shared global challenges.</p><p>What to watch: The outcomes of these high-level discussions and their implications for international cooperation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately reflects source; no extraneous claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
