       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-09-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Warning To Taliban's Supreme Leader? Why Has Pakistan Renewed Strikes On Afghanistan</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world news</span> <span>#Pakistan</span> <span>#Afghanistan</span> <span>#Taliban</span></div>
       <p>Pakistan has carried out a strike on Kandahar, a city recognized as a significant stronghold for the Taliban leadership. This action also targets a location known to be the home of Akhundzada, the Taliban's supreme leader. The bombardment marks a notable escalation in regional tensions, as it is the first confirmed Pakistani strike on Kandahar since March.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/warning-to-talibans-supreme-leader-why-has-pakistan-renewed-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The military action signals a potential shift in Pakistan's approach to border security or its relationship with the Taliban government in Afghanistan. Kandahar's strategic importance as a center for the Taliban's command and control makes any military engagement there particularly sensitive and carries significant symbolic weight. The timing and target selection suggest a deliberate and calculated move by Pakistan.</p><p>This development follows a period of several months without direct Pakistani military operations within the city of Kandahar. The renewal of strikes raises immediate questions about the underlying reasons and immediate objectives of Pakistan's military policy towards Afghanistan, especially concerning cross-border security challenges. Regional observers and international bodies will be closely watching for further details regarding the nature of the strike and any subsequent reactions from the Taliban or the broader international community.</p><p>What to watch: Official statements from Pakistan and the Taliban, and potential ripple effects on regional stability.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly captures the significance and context of the strike mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/warning-to-talibans-supreme-leader-why-has-pakistan-renewed-strikes-on-afghanistan-ws-l-10351556.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
