     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-09-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>'While he is not playing, I am pretty happy to captain Australia in ODIs' - Mitchell Marsh on Pat Cummins' absence in 1st ODI vs South Africa</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Australia</span> <span>#South Africa</span> <span>#ODI</span></div>
       <p>Australia's cricketing landscape sees a temporary leadership change as Mitchell Marsh steps up to captain the side in the opening One-Day International against South Africa. This development comes as regular skipper Pat Cummins is sidelined, managing his workload in anticipation of the upcoming Test series. Marsh's comments reflect a readiness for the role, stating his happiness to lead the team in Cummins' absence.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-24/while-he-is-not-playing-i-am-pretty-happy-to-captain-austral.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The decision to rest Cummins highlights a strategic approach by the Australian management, prioritizing the fitness and readiness of key players for the demanding Test schedule ahead. With an important Test series on the horizon, ensuring Cummins is in optimal condition is paramount, leading to his planned absence from this initial ODI fixture.</p><p>For the touring Australian squad, the first ODI against South Africa presents an early challenge and an opportunity for players to solidify their positions. Marsh's captaincy will be under scrutiny, as he aims to guide the team to a strong start in the series. The match also allows other squad members to step up and demonstrate their capabilities in the absence of a senior player like Cummins. The series context suggests careful planning around player availability.</p><p>What to watch: How Marsh leads the team and the performance of Australian players in Cummins' absence.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly captures the context of the source, including the reason for Cummins' absence and Marsh's captaincy.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/while-he-is-not-playing-i-am-pretty-happy-to-captain-australia-in-odis-mitchell-marsh-on-pat-cummins-absence-in-1st-odi-vs-south-africa/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
